🌟 StarPulse
Astronaut Health Monitoring & Early Warning System

NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026 | Create Health Monitoring Software for Astronauts on Space Missions

Monitoring astronaut health, one pulse at a time.

🚀 Overview

StarPulse is an astronaut-centered health monitoring platform that collects, visualizes, and analyzes physiological and wellness data during space missions.

The system gives astronauts a centralized dashboard to monitor daily health and spot potential complications before they escalate.


🧑‍💻 Running the demo app

The app is React + Vite + TypeScript. You need Node 18 or newer.

    npm install
    npm run dev

Then open the address it prints (usually http://localhost:5173).

- Screens: Health tracking (5 area views), daily check-in, 12 stat detail pages, Rewards, Crew, Alerts.
- All data is mock data in src/data/mockData.ts. Edit values there to change what the app shows.
- Anything you log is saved in your browser only. To start over, click the JH avatar → "Reset demo data".
- Design tokens (colors, type, spacing) come from the Figma style guide and live in src/styles/tokens.css.
